{
    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "LGCIP30_CONUS_001",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The Global Food Security-support Analysis Data ([GFSAD](https://www.usgs.gov/centers/western-geographic-science-center/science/global-food-and-water-security-support-analysis)) project provides global cropland datasets to help address food and water security challenges of the twenty-first century. The project develops multiple cropland products using time series of Landsat and Sentinel-2 satellite data, machine learning algorithms, and cloud computing.\n\nThe GFSAD Landsat-derived Global Cropland Intensity Product of the Conterminous United States for the year 2020 (nominal) 30 meters (m) Version 001 (LGCIP30_CONUS) maps seven classes of cropland intensity. The Level 3 product was derived from Harmonized Landsat and Sentinel-2 ([HLS](https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/data/projects/hls)) time series data for the period 2019-2021 to create a nominal 2020 product.\n\nThe LGCIP30_CONUS data product contains one variable representing cropland intensity with the following seven classes: Water/Ocean, Single Cropped croplands, Double Cropped croplands, Triple Cropped croplands (not utilized for CONUS), Continuous croplands, Fallow croplands, and Non-croplands. The data product is provided in Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF (COG) format as 10\u00b0 x 10\u00b0 tiles. A low-resolution browse image is also available.\n\nCurrently, the LGCIP30 product is only available for the Conterminous United States. LGCIP30 data covering the rest of the planet will be added at a later date.",
